1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,437 --> 00:00:21,604
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,986 --> 00:00:29,863
[Julio] <i>I'm here to make you</i>
<i>an offer, Ivy.</i>

6
00:00:29,946 --> 00:00:32,907
<i>-A hundred million pesos.</i>
<i>-In exchange for?</i>

7
00:00:32,991 --> 00:00:33,950
<i>Get back together with my grandson.</i>

8
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:35,201
[Camia] <i>What are you going to do?</i>

9
00:00:35,285 --> 00:00:39,039
<i>Help Arnaldo recover</i>
<i>right after having him jailed?</i>

10
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:41,624
<i>Arnaldo is the weakness of the Ardientes--</i>

11
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:44,669
<i>Emilia, Raul, and especially Julio.</i>

12
00:00:44,753 --> 00:00:49,632
<i>So I need Arnaldo to finish off</i>
<i>the Ardientes once and for all.</i>

13
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:54,345
[Julio] <i>Ivy Aguas' funeral is</i>
<i>postponed until further notice.</i>

14
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:55,388
[screaming]

15
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:56,806
-[Raul] <i>What's going on?</i>
-<i>Nothing!</i>

16
00:00:56,890 --> 00:01:00,643
<i>I need a man who is my equal,</i>
<i>and that obviously isn't you!</i>

17
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:02,228
[Raul] <i>Well then, let's split up already!</i>

18
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:04,773
[Julio] <i>Your son needs you</i>
<i>all the more right now!</i>

19
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:06,775
<i>And I don't want the public to know</i>

20
00:01:06,858 --> 00:01:09,486
<i>that this family is already falling apart!</i>

21
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:13,239
[Camia] <i>Mayor Arnaldo's release</i>
<i>is a slap in the face</i>

22
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:15,408
<i>to the people of Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

23
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:18,661
<i>Only one man has the right</i>
<i>to lead Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

24
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:20,330
<i>That's Diego Torillo.</i>

25
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:22,874
[supporters] <i>Diego Torillo for change!</i>

26
00:01:22,957 --> 00:01:25,210
<i>Let the games begin!</i>

27
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:27,796
[Ivy] <i>You just think you've won, Emilia.</i>

28
00:01:27,879 --> 00:01:31,758
<i>But it was all part of my plan.</i>

29
00:01:31,841 --> 00:01:34,886
<i>Ivy's here. When you find her, kill her.</i>

30
00:01:34,969 --> 00:01:37,430
<i>We'll make it look like an accident.</i>

31
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:41,559
[tires screeching]

32
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:46,189
[suspenseful music playing]

33
00:01:47,899 --> 00:01:49,150
[Emilia shrieking]

34
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:51,861
You-- Ivy!

35
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:01,204
Where were you?!

36
00:02:01,287 --> 00:02:04,165
Look, she's escaped! Ouch!

37
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:06,000
-[groans]
-[woman] Emilia, what happened?!

38
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:09,546
Guard, where are
the surveillance cameras here?

39
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:10,505
This way, ma'am.

40
00:02:10,588 --> 00:02:13,174
I'll make sure that woman pays for this!

41
00:02:15,385 --> 00:02:16,553
[growls]

42
00:02:16,636 --> 00:02:18,638
[tense music playing]

43
00:02:19,305 --> 00:02:21,850
[ominous music playing]

44
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:23,143
[Jaguar] We can't be sure yet

45
00:02:23,226 --> 00:02:25,478
of Diego's victory in the election.

46
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:30,316
The Ardientes will do everything
in their power to make sure

47
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:33,570
that their territory
doesn't fall into enemy hands.

48
00:02:34,779 --> 00:02:38,867
Boss, how can Mayor Arnaldo
still win at this point?

49
00:02:39,117 --> 00:02:40,368
He's gone insane.

50
00:02:41,369 --> 00:02:44,747
A lot of people have lost their sanity

51
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:47,125
after being elected in this town.

52
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:50,962
I've yet to hear a corpse
getting elected though.

53
00:02:52,171 --> 00:02:55,884
But that just might happen to Diego…

54
00:02:56,217 --> 00:02:58,303
if you fail to protect him.

55
00:02:58,386 --> 00:03:00,138
If we fail to protect him!

56
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:04,851
I must acquire the Ardientes'
power at all costs.

57
00:03:05,476 --> 00:03:10,023
And that'll only happen
if Diego wins the election.

58
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:13,359
If you manage to protect him, that is.

59
00:03:15,403 --> 00:03:16,279
Madrigal…

60
00:03:17,322 --> 00:03:19,824
You'll be my eyes
and ears in Diego's camp.

61
00:03:20,992 --> 00:03:26,497
Make sure nothing bad happens
to him, or else, it's on you.

62
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:30,126
Leave it to me, boss. As you wish.

63
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:38,092
[tense music playing]

64
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:45,808
Looks like there's no footage
of the culprit, ma'am Emilia.

65
00:03:45,892 --> 00:03:48,645
Whoever did this planned
everything in advance.

66
00:03:48,728 --> 00:03:51,064
They knew where
the camera's blind spots were,

67
00:03:51,147 --> 00:03:52,315
and how to avoid the guards.

68
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:54,901
There's no proof it was Ivy Aguas.

69
00:03:54,984 --> 00:03:55,902
[grunts]

70
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:58,655
[breathing heavily]

71
00:03:59,781 --> 00:04:01,074
[guard] We're sorry, ma'am.

72
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:08,081
[lamp switch flicking]

73
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:11,000
[lamp switch flicking]

74
00:04:15,421 --> 00:04:18,549
[lamp switch flicking]

75
00:04:23,346 --> 00:04:24,347
Arnaldo.

76
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:27,308
[lamp switch flicking]

77
00:04:29,185 --> 00:04:30,186
Arnal--

78
00:04:34,565 --> 00:04:35,692
Arnaldo…

79
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:41,572
Arnaldo, what are you doing there?

80
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:45,118
[lamp switch flicking]

81
00:04:48,079 --> 00:04:50,248
Arnaldo, come here.

82
00:04:51,416 --> 00:04:54,002
Arnaldo, it's me, your grandfather.

83
00:04:55,586 --> 00:04:57,338
Come here and take your medicine.

84
00:04:58,298 --> 00:04:59,465
Come on.

85
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:02,844
This is me, your Grandpa Julio.

86
00:05:05,513 --> 00:05:09,058
Come here. Take your medicine.

87
00:05:09,475 --> 00:05:10,393
That's it.

88
00:05:15,106 --> 00:05:16,482
Come on, son.

89
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,234
Please.

90
00:05:21,988 --> 00:05:23,072
That's it.

91
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:28,911
Take your medicine. This is good for you.

92
00:05:31,122 --> 00:05:32,123
Hmm?

93
00:05:34,625 --> 00:05:38,629
[somber music playing]

94
00:05:47,305 --> 00:05:48,765
Arnaldo, Arnaldo!

95
00:05:49,015 --> 00:05:51,059
Arnaldo! Arnaldo!

96
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:53,519
-Arnaldo, that's enough!
-[chuckling]

97
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:55,646
-[chuckling]
-Arnaldo…

98
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:56,898
You're not insane.

99
00:05:57,857 --> 00:05:59,692
You're not crazy. Do you hear me?

100
00:06:00,943 --> 00:06:02,487
I won't let you go insane.

101
00:06:03,196 --> 00:06:06,866
I made you a god of this place.

102
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:11,204
I won't let you throw away
everything I've done for you.

103
00:06:12,038 --> 00:06:13,331
Arnaldo…

104
00:06:13,581 --> 00:06:15,625
[singing indistinctly]

105
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:18,795
Arnaldo, please.

106
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:21,547
Do you hear me?

107
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:23,841
[pills clatter softly]

108
00:06:25,009 --> 00:06:30,306
I… V… Y…

109
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:34,769
A… G… U…

110
00:06:34,852 --> 00:06:36,229
…as.

111
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:40,650
I… V…

112
00:06:42,777 --> 00:06:43,778
Y…

113
00:06:45,363 --> 00:06:48,699
I… V…

114
00:06:50,576 --> 00:06:51,869
-Y…
-[Julio sighs]

115
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:57,750
Aguas. [laughing]

116
00:07:01,087 --> 00:07:04,173
I! V! Y!

117
00:07:04,257 --> 00:07:09,345
A! G! U! A! S!

118
00:07:09,428 --> 00:07:13,015
I! V! Y!

119
00:07:13,641 --> 00:07:19,063
A! G! U! A! S!

120
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:21,607
Enough… Enough!

121
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:23,359
Enough…

122
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:25,570
-You'll come back.
-That's enough, Arnaldo.

123
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:26,946
You'll come back to me.

124
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,073
-[sniffles]
-[Arnaldo] A…

125
00:07:29,157 --> 00:07:30,741
This is my fault.

126
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:34,036
-G… U…
-It's my fault.

127
00:07:34,662 --> 00:07:38,166
[whispering] A… G…

128
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:41,085
U… A…

129
00:07:42,336 --> 00:07:43,504
S…

130
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:47,550
I… V…

131
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:50,136
[chortles]

132
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:55,558
Please, stop it…

133
00:07:57,810 --> 00:08:01,564
[chortling continues]

134
00:08:03,065 --> 00:08:05,943
-Damn you, Ivy!
-[chortling continues]

135
00:08:07,695 --> 00:08:10,531
Damn you, Ivy Aguas!

136
00:08:11,073 --> 00:08:14,160
-What have you done to my son?
-[chortling continues]

137
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:17,997
I'm not done with you, Ivy!

138
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:21,125
I am not yet done with you.

139
00:08:21,709 --> 00:08:25,213
[tense music playing]

140
00:08:28,966 --> 00:08:30,051
Dear.

141
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:35,264
[somber music playing]

142
00:08:37,934 --> 00:08:40,770
I'm sure the Ardientes
are already coming up

143
00:08:40,853 --> 00:08:42,605
with a way to silence you.

144
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:46,484
I'm not afraid of them at all.

145
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:48,986
And I don't have to hide
behind you, either.

146
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:52,073
Don't go back to the Ardientes anymore.

147
00:08:52,156 --> 00:08:54,659
Let me fight against them now.

148
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:56,911
Please, come home.

149
00:08:56,994 --> 00:08:58,120
Mom, I'm sorry.

150
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:01,916
But I'll be able to protect you more

151
00:09:01,999 --> 00:09:03,501
if I stay close with the Ardientes.

152
00:09:03,584 --> 00:09:08,089
[pensive music playing]

153
00:09:29,068 --> 00:09:32,154
Mayor, I brought you some food.

154
00:09:32,989 --> 00:09:33,990
Mayor?

155
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:35,491
Mayor?

156
00:09:36,492 --> 00:09:39,620
-[ominous music playing]
-[plates and utensils clatter]

157
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:41,998
Mayor!

158
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:44,208
Ma'am Emilia!

159
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:46,210
Ma'am Emilia!

160
00:09:46,294 --> 00:09:47,712
-Ma'am Emilia!
-Arnaldo?!

161
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:48,879
[house help] Ma'am!

162
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:50,506
-What happened?!
-Ma'am Emilia!

163
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:51,716
-What's going on?!
-Arnaldo!

164
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:53,926
[ominous music playing]

165
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:55,303
[Julio] What happened?!

166
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:57,221
[shrieking]

167
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:01,309
[both shrieking]

168
00:10:01,392 --> 00:10:03,019
Arnaldo! Arnaldo!

169
00:10:03,644 --> 00:10:05,646
[shrieking]

170
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:07,023
Arnaldo!

171
00:10:08,482 --> 00:10:10,735
[Raul] Help! Papa!

172
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:12,069
Arnaldo!

173
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:15,740
-[gunshots]
-[Raul] Son!

174
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:20,161
Son! [screams]

175
00:10:20,244 --> 00:10:21,329
Arnaldo!

176
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:22,913
Arnaldo!

177
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:24,540
-[Emilia wails]
-[Raul screams]

178
00:10:24,624 --> 00:10:26,042
[Raul] Arnaldo!

179
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:28,252
-[Emilia sobs] Arnaldo!
-[Raul] Help!

180
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:31,422
Help…

181
00:10:31,505 --> 00:10:34,216
-[Raul screams]
-[Emilia wailing]

182
00:10:36,552 --> 00:10:39,764
-[Raul] Arnaldo! Help!
-[Emilia wailing]

183
00:10:41,557 --> 00:10:42,767
Son!

184
00:10:44,393 --> 00:10:46,896
[desolate music playing]

185
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:51,275
[Emilia wailing]

186
00:10:51,942 --> 00:10:53,027
[Raul] Son!

187
00:10:53,653 --> 00:10:54,695
Son!

188
00:10:54,779 --> 00:10:56,530
[Emilia wailing]

189
00:10:58,574 --> 00:11:00,159
Arnaldo…

190
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:04,914
Why? Why?

191
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:07,375
-[Raul] Get help!
-Why?

192
00:11:07,458 --> 00:11:10,211
[sobbing] Arnaldo!

193
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:13,130
-Please! Get help!
-[Emilia] Arnaldo!

194
00:11:13,756 --> 00:11:16,425
-[Raul] Son? Arnaldo!
-[Emilia] Arnaldo!

195
00:11:17,134 --> 00:11:19,178
Arnaldo!

196
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:32,775
[desolate music playing]

197
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:53,379
[desolate music playing]

198
00:12:10,938 --> 00:12:11,939
Miss Ivy?

199
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:15,401
Please wait here.
I'll call the congressman.

200
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:17,111
What happened?

201
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:19,113
Excuse me. [sniffles]

202
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:30,583
[desolate music playing]

203
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:11,540
[Julio sniffling]

204
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:15,336
[foreboding music playing]

205
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:30,643
[whimpering]

206
00:13:36,106 --> 00:13:39,151
[sobbing]

207
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:49,245
[stirring music playing]

208
00:13:49,328 --> 00:13:51,789
[sobs] Look. Look…

209
00:13:52,957 --> 00:13:55,292
Look what happened to Arnaldo…

210
00:13:56,669 --> 00:14:00,005
Look what happened to my grandson!

211
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:03,092
He hung himself! [sobs]

212
00:14:03,175 --> 00:14:05,469
[tense music playing]

213
00:14:05,553 --> 00:14:08,847
[sobbing]

214
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:16,522
<i>Who did this to you?!</i>

215
00:14:17,731 --> 00:14:21,026
<i>Who?! </i>[wailing]

216
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:23,529
<i>Mark my words,</i>

217
00:14:23,612 --> 00:14:28,325
<i>you'll meet the same fate</i>
<i>as Nanny Carlotta did.</i>

218
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:34,331
<i>I'll make you suffer so much</i>
<i>you'll want to kill yourself.</i>

219
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:40,963
He hung himself, Ivy… He hung himself.

220
00:14:41,046 --> 00:14:44,174
[Julio sobbing]

221
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:46,594
Why? Why?

222
00:14:47,011 --> 00:14:49,096
Why did he do it?

223
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:53,100
[sobbing]

224
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:57,813
[sobs]

225
00:14:58,314 --> 00:14:59,815
Why…

226
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,317
Why?

227
00:15:03,861 --> 00:15:06,071
[sobbing continues]

228
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:17,374
[sobs] My poor grandson…

229
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:20,753
[sobbing continues]

230
00:15:22,546 --> 00:15:24,757
<i>I'm not an evil person.</i>

231
00:15:25,507 --> 00:15:29,094
<i>But your family drove me</i>
<i>to become like this.</i>

232
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:33,057
<i>I must put an end to your cruelty…</i>

233
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:37,019
<i>so that no one else will have to</i>
<i>experience hell at your hands.</i>

234
00:15:37,811 --> 00:15:39,939
<i>This is the only law I know…</i>

235
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:42,775
<i>Do not do unto others</i>

236
00:15:42,858 --> 00:15:45,527
<i>what you don't want others to do unto you.</i>

237
00:15:46,570 --> 00:15:47,988
[sobbing]

238
00:15:56,038 --> 00:15:59,041
[tense music playing]

239
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:02,211
[sobbing]

240
00:16:02,544 --> 00:16:03,545
[sniffles]

241
00:16:11,845 --> 00:16:13,347
[whimpering]

242
00:16:18,227 --> 00:16:20,938
No respectable man

243
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:26,860
is ever prepared for the worst
that can happen

244
00:16:26,944 --> 00:16:29,154
to his flesh and blood.

245
00:16:32,032 --> 00:16:35,661
Ivy, Arnaldo is in the hospital…

246
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:39,873
He's in the hospital
and he's fighting for his life!

247
00:16:39,957 --> 00:16:41,875
[sobbing]

248
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:43,502
[Emilia] Arnaldo!

249
00:16:44,169 --> 00:16:47,172
[Claire] Don't worry… He'll be fine.

250
00:16:48,382 --> 00:16:51,176
[screams] Where's the doctor?! Doctor!

251
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,720
[Raul] Doc, this is an emergency!

252
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:53,971
Please attend to my son!

253
00:16:54,513 --> 00:16:56,640
Doc, please do everything to save our son!

254
00:16:58,350 --> 00:17:00,227
[sobbing]

255
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:04,148
[Emilia sobbing]

256
00:17:07,901 --> 00:17:10,612
Arnaldo! [sobbing]

257
00:17:10,696 --> 00:17:12,197
-[doctor] Check vitals.
-Yes, doc.

258
00:17:12,823 --> 00:17:16,160
[sobbing] Arnaldo…

259
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:19,163
You mean… Arnaldo's still alive?

260
00:17:19,455 --> 00:17:22,541
But he's fighting for his life!
Do you understand?!

261
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:24,960
He's fighting for his life!

262
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:27,296
[Julio sobbing]

263
00:17:27,379 --> 00:17:30,924
[tense music playing]

264
00:17:34,344 --> 00:17:35,637
You know, Auntie,

265
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:38,932
even if Arnaldo and I
don't always get along,

266
00:17:39,016 --> 00:17:42,644
he's still my son and I'm going
to do everything to protect him.

267
00:17:43,687 --> 00:17:45,355
We just need to trust and believe

268
00:17:45,439 --> 00:17:48,901
that Arnaldo can survive
all of this. Okay?

269
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:51,820
[tense music playing]

270
00:18:04,625 --> 00:18:05,501
You!

271
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:07,377
Emilia, don't. Don't.

272
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:09,922
What makes you think for
a second that I won't find out

273
00:18:10,005 --> 00:18:11,298
the little stunt that you pulled?

274
00:18:12,216 --> 00:18:14,551
You have some nerve. Stay there!

275
00:18:14,843 --> 00:18:19,556
I have no time to fight.
I'm here for Arnaldo.

276
00:18:21,308 --> 00:18:23,936
You tormented him. You left him!

277
00:18:24,019 --> 00:18:28,357
And now you're visiting him?
You have some nerve, huh?!

278
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,441
Get out.

279
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:31,151
-Get--
-Don't touch me.

280
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:35,447
Emilia?

281
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:46,917
Don't you dare go near my son.
We aren't done yet.

282
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:51,630
[tense music playing]

283
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:00,514
[Emilia shrieking]

284
00:19:00,597 --> 00:19:01,723
[Raul] <i>Arnaldo!</i>

285
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:02,975
[gunshot]

286
00:19:04,601 --> 00:19:06,395
<i>Arnaldo! Son!</i>

287
00:19:07,813 --> 00:19:11,441
[unsettling music playing]

288
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:13,068
[phone ringing]

289
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:15,904
[phone ringing]

290
00:19:17,197 --> 00:19:18,615
[phone ringing]

291
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:21,869
[phone continues ringing]

292
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:32,045
<i>Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo</i>
<i>was rushed to the hospital</i>

293
00:19:32,129 --> 00:19:36,175
<i>earlier this afternoon</i>
<i>due to unknown reasons.</i>

294
00:19:36,258 --> 00:19:39,845
<i>According to witnesses,</i>
<i>the mayor was unconscious</i>

295
00:19:39,928 --> 00:19:42,472
<i>when he was rushed</i>
<i>to the Ardiente Medical Center.</i>

296
00:19:42,556 --> 00:19:46,476
<i>We have yet to confirm</i>
<i>the mayor's condition…</i>

297
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:49,271
What kind of stunt is this?

298
00:19:50,063 --> 00:19:52,191
[reporter] <i>Will the mayor</i>
<i>soon give up his campaign</i>

299
00:19:52,274 --> 00:19:53,692
<i>and let his brother, Diego, win?</i>

300
00:19:53,775 --> 00:19:55,777
<i>We'll return for more updates.</i>

301
00:19:55,861 --> 00:19:58,906
<i>This is Dennis Pangilinan, reporting.</i>

302
00:20:02,784 --> 00:20:05,204
[Julio] <i>No way in hell</i>

303
00:20:05,787 --> 00:20:10,751
will I allow a bastard like Diego

304
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:14,880
to think that he can defeat Arnaldo.

305
00:20:17,591 --> 00:20:20,761
Ardientes are born winners.

306
00:20:22,137 --> 00:20:25,390
An Ardiente never dies!

307
00:20:26,892 --> 00:20:33,690
An Ardiente never loses or accepts defeat.

308
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:42,241
[tense music playing]

309
00:20:45,410 --> 00:20:46,370
[clatters]

310
00:20:54,002 --> 00:20:56,171
Arnaldo's hanging was near fatal.

311
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:58,548
It's lucky that you found him right away.

312
00:20:59,049 --> 00:21:00,300
Doc, can we see him?

313
00:21:01,051 --> 00:21:03,262
The patient is still in critical care.

314
00:21:03,762 --> 00:21:06,098
His airway is secured by intubation.

315
00:21:06,181 --> 00:21:08,725
We will perform some tests to make sure

316
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:11,603
the patient didn't sustain
any major injuries.

317
00:21:12,562 --> 00:21:13,981
Thank you, doc.

318
00:21:14,523 --> 00:21:15,524
Excuse me.

319
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:17,567
Thank you.

320
00:21:18,193 --> 00:21:19,444
That's good news.

321
00:21:19,528 --> 00:21:22,531
[tense music playing]

322
00:21:27,327 --> 00:21:28,245
[sighs]

323
00:21:33,458 --> 00:21:34,501
[door opens]

324
00:21:37,421 --> 00:21:40,966
[monitor beeping rhythmically]

325
00:21:48,098 --> 00:21:52,102
[ominous music playing]

326
00:22:08,785 --> 00:22:12,914
[suspenseful music playing]

327
00:22:15,042 --> 00:22:17,210
Do you want me to pity you?

328
00:22:21,006 --> 00:22:24,760
My heart is incapable
of pitying you though.

329
00:22:28,513 --> 00:22:31,016
Because every time I look at you…

330
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:38,899
I remember all the things you've done.

331
00:22:42,569 --> 00:22:45,739
So, even if I want you to experience

332
00:22:47,074 --> 00:22:50,827
all the pain you've inflicted
on my loved ones

333
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:54,873
and to all the families you've ruined…

334
00:23:01,713 --> 00:23:04,049
I can't let you die just yet.

335
00:23:08,637 --> 00:23:13,225
Because you don't deserve to die, Arnaldo.

336
00:23:13,308 --> 00:23:15,602
You deserve a fate worse than death.

337
00:23:15,685 --> 00:23:18,146
[suspenseful music playing]

338
00:23:20,482 --> 00:23:22,317
You need to live.

339
00:23:26,863 --> 00:23:29,741
Because I'm not done with you yet.

340
00:23:29,825 --> 00:23:33,662
I'm not through with the Ardientes.

341
00:23:34,621 --> 00:23:37,332
Get that Ivy Aguas out of my son's room!

342
00:23:37,415 --> 00:23:38,333
I don't want to see her!

343
00:23:38,416 --> 00:23:41,086
-I want her out of my sight now!
-[Julio] Emilia!

344
00:23:42,504 --> 00:23:45,674
How could you be so careless?!

345
00:23:46,216 --> 00:23:49,302
Now the whole world knows
what happened to Arnaldo!

346
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:52,139
-Papa, I banned the media here!
-[chuckles]

347
00:23:52,222 --> 00:23:53,056
I got news for you!

348
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:58,436
The news was leaked and it
landed on national television!

349
00:24:00,355 --> 00:24:02,274
Miss Aguas, please come with me.

350
00:24:04,526 --> 00:24:06,653
No, I'll stay with Arnaldo.

351
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:09,281
But Miss Emilia doesn't want you in here--

352
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:11,908
I don't care.

353
00:24:12,409 --> 00:24:15,036
You truly are useless.

354
00:24:15,537 --> 00:24:16,830
Useless?

355
00:24:16,913 --> 00:24:18,456
I'm the one who's useless, Papa?

356
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:21,626
Who was with Arnaldo while
he was hanging for his life?

357
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:23,628
When he was being revived? It was me!

358
00:24:23,712 --> 00:24:24,838
And you tell me I'm useless?

359
00:24:24,921 --> 00:24:26,923
This is all your fault, Papa!

360
00:24:28,049 --> 00:24:29,968
[Julio] I have never…

361
00:24:30,051 --> 00:24:35,974
nor will I ever do anything
that will ruin my grandson.

362
00:24:36,057 --> 00:24:40,270
Arnaldo will get well
and he will become governor.

363
00:24:40,353 --> 00:24:41,771
Honestly, you're the only one

364
00:24:41,855 --> 00:24:43,690
who's not doing anything for your son

365
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:45,817
except to usurp his candidacy!

366
00:24:45,901 --> 00:24:48,737
I wanted to run for governor
not because of my ambition,

367
00:24:48,820 --> 00:24:51,615
but because I know
that my son is not well!

368
00:24:51,698 --> 00:24:54,492
He needs to heal and rest!
But what did you do?

369
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:56,828
You treated him like he just had a fever!

370
00:24:56,912 --> 00:24:59,206
Like he'd get better
just by drinking some medicine!

371
00:24:59,289 --> 00:25:00,332
That's not it, Papa!

372
00:25:00,415 --> 00:25:03,585
You have to accept the fact
that Arnaldo is not well!

373
00:25:03,668 --> 00:25:05,587
You're the one who's killing him--

374
00:25:06,463 --> 00:25:07,339
[Raul] Papa!

375
00:25:07,422 --> 00:25:10,634
-Julio, what are you doing?!
-Shut up, all of you!

376
00:25:10,717 --> 00:25:12,093
No one!

377
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:15,055
No one tells Julio Ardiente what to do!

378
00:25:16,097 --> 00:25:18,016
You know why I'm forcing Arnaldo

379
00:25:18,099 --> 00:25:22,395
to get over this temporary
mental incapacity?

380
00:25:22,479 --> 00:25:24,731
It's because if I were to leave it to you,

381
00:25:25,357 --> 00:25:26,816
we wouldn't gain anything!

382
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:29,527
The Ardientes wouldn't
accomplish anything!

383
00:25:30,278 --> 00:25:33,240
You entourage of freeloaders!

384
00:25:36,159 --> 00:25:36,993
And you!

385
00:25:38,787 --> 00:25:41,248
Get your filthy hands off her,

386
00:25:41,873 --> 00:25:45,043
and wrap those fingers
around the neck of the person

387
00:25:45,126 --> 00:25:48,129
who ordered you to throw Ivy Aguas out!

388
00:25:48,213 --> 00:25:52,384
Ivy Aguas is here to stay at my behest!

389
00:25:53,843 --> 00:25:56,012
That's the end of this conversation!

390
00:26:01,184 --> 00:26:05,146
[tense music playing]

391
00:26:11,486 --> 00:26:12,737
Emilia, let's go.

392
00:26:16,866 --> 00:26:20,870
[tense music playing]

393
00:26:26,459 --> 00:26:29,004
Auntie, does Ivy know
what happened to Arnaldo?

394
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:33,842
Diego, Lily returned to the Ardientes.

395
00:26:34,718 --> 00:26:35,719
What?!

396
00:26:37,762 --> 00:26:40,098
She needs to finish what she started,

397
00:26:40,432 --> 00:26:43,643
even if it means putting off our reunion.

398
00:26:43,727 --> 00:26:48,982
[sighs] Auntie, I don't want to
lose faith in Ivy's decisions.

399
00:26:49,566 --> 00:26:50,817
But it's too dangerous!

400
00:26:50,900 --> 00:26:53,486
What if this time, she can't
escape the Ardientes anymore?

401
00:26:55,238 --> 00:26:56,239
[sighs]

402
00:26:57,365 --> 00:27:00,160
She always puts her life in danger.

403
00:27:07,876 --> 00:27:10,795
Has it ever happened in your life…

404
00:27:11,713 --> 00:27:14,799
that you felt your life

405
00:27:14,883 --> 00:27:20,764
was being toyed around
by some unseen force…

406
00:27:20,847 --> 00:27:24,601
and you felt so helpless
that you couldn't do anything?

407
00:27:25,643 --> 00:27:29,105
[tense music playing]

408
00:27:29,189 --> 00:27:30,982
I have.

409
00:27:32,484 --> 00:27:34,819
Lots of times, Congressman.

410
00:27:36,654 --> 00:27:38,615
In our lives,

411
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:45,580
some things happen
when you least expect them to.

412
00:27:46,373 --> 00:27:50,377
That's why, you take control
of the situation,

413
00:27:51,753 --> 00:27:54,339
and use it to your advantage.

414
00:27:56,216 --> 00:27:57,842
What about you, Congressman?

415
00:27:58,802 --> 00:27:59,886
[sighs]

416
00:28:00,470 --> 00:28:01,554
Never.

417
00:28:02,097 --> 00:28:04,349
[chuckles] That has never
happened to me before.

418
00:28:04,432 --> 00:28:05,558
[Julio inhales sharply]

419
00:28:05,975 --> 00:28:10,146
They say that all the
wrong things you've done

420
00:28:10,230 --> 00:28:12,440
will come back to you.

421
00:28:12,899 --> 00:28:17,153
Well, I spit on karma's grave.

422
00:28:19,489 --> 00:28:20,990
I have the power.

423
00:28:23,159 --> 00:28:28,081
Karma has always been
just a concept in my life…

424
00:28:28,832 --> 00:28:29,874
…until now.

425
00:28:32,544 --> 00:28:36,881
I will face anything or anyone.

426
00:28:37,715 --> 00:28:39,342
Even the Devil himself.

427
00:28:40,051 --> 00:28:42,637
I will face him and say,

428
00:28:43,430 --> 00:28:45,890
"You can take my life…

429
00:28:48,059 --> 00:28:50,562
in exchange for Arnaldo's."

430
00:28:53,857 --> 00:28:56,818
[monitor beeping rhythmically]

431
00:28:56,901 --> 00:29:01,030
[somber music playing]

432
00:29:03,116 --> 00:29:05,702
I can't believe the gut of that witch!

433
00:29:05,785 --> 00:29:07,078
She has the nerve to come here

434
00:29:07,162 --> 00:29:08,747
after everything she did to Arnaldo!

435
00:29:08,830 --> 00:29:11,499
How shameless! She even
got Papa under her spell!

436
00:29:12,083 --> 00:29:14,252
Maybe Ivy is just worried about Arnaldo.

437
00:29:14,335 --> 00:29:16,212
Those two loved each other back then.

438
00:29:16,296 --> 00:29:20,383
So maybe we could cut Ivy some slack,

439
00:29:20,467 --> 00:29:22,635
and give her another chance for Arnaldo.

440
00:29:23,595 --> 00:29:24,679
Hold on.

441
00:29:25,597 --> 00:29:27,640
Are you sure you're referring
to Ivy and Arnaldo?

442
00:29:27,724 --> 00:29:30,310
Because I don't have the time
to listen to your drama, Raul.

443
00:29:30,769 --> 00:29:32,687
That Ivy… [scoffs]

444
00:29:32,771 --> 00:29:34,731
Everything is her fault.

445
00:29:34,814 --> 00:29:38,193
She put Arnaldo under her spell
until he went crazy.

446
00:29:38,276 --> 00:29:39,486
I know it.

447
00:29:39,569 --> 00:29:40,612
But I promise you,

448
00:29:40,695 --> 00:29:43,364
she'll never be able
to set foot in our house.

449
00:29:43,448 --> 00:29:45,074
[exhales] She'll pay for everything.

450
00:29:48,453 --> 00:29:49,788
Raul, please!

451
00:29:53,708 --> 00:29:55,460
You know, Congressman…

452
00:29:56,711 --> 00:29:59,672
Arnaldo is very important to me.

453
00:30:05,887 --> 00:30:08,598
So, while you're here in the hospital…

454
00:30:11,100 --> 00:30:13,144
I will stay with you…

455
00:30:13,853 --> 00:30:15,605
until he recovers.

456
00:30:19,984 --> 00:30:21,611
I have decided.

457
00:30:23,279 --> 00:30:25,573
I will get back together with Arnaldo.

458
00:30:29,953 --> 00:30:31,996
And I will take care of him.

459
00:30:38,711 --> 00:30:39,712
[sniffles]

460
00:30:40,129 --> 00:30:44,592
Then--Then I will have the money prepared.

461
00:30:44,884 --> 00:30:46,010
But, wait…

462
00:30:46,386 --> 00:30:52,058
You haven't told me which
position you're interested in.

463
00:30:52,642 --> 00:30:55,770
Livelihood? Uh, health?

464
00:30:59,232 --> 00:31:00,441
Miss Aguas…

465
00:31:00,692 --> 00:31:06,197
Julio Ardiente always keeps his promises.

466
00:31:10,368 --> 00:31:11,870
I know that.

467
00:31:14,455 --> 00:31:17,083
But Arnaldo is more important to me.

468
00:31:17,625 --> 00:31:22,213
I don't need money
or any government position.

469
00:31:29,679 --> 00:31:32,056
Do you mean to tell me…

470
00:31:34,642 --> 00:31:39,814
love is a good enough reason for you?

471
00:31:40,523 --> 00:31:41,608
[inhales sharply]

472
00:31:41,691 --> 00:31:44,027
Arnaldo is important to me…

473
00:31:45,820 --> 00:31:48,698
so I will take care of him.

474
00:31:48,948 --> 00:31:52,952
[tense music playing]

475
00:31:59,083 --> 00:32:04,255
<i>I lied, pretended, and made</i>
<i>heavy choices out of anger.</i>

476
00:32:04,339 --> 00:32:05,965
<i>But we're still different</i>

477
00:32:06,049 --> 00:32:07,842
<i>when it comes to who or what we turn to.</i>

478
00:32:08,927 --> 00:32:11,512
<i>May my loved ones forgive and guide me…</i>

479
00:32:12,055 --> 00:32:15,767
<i>because I will never give up this fight.</i>

480
00:32:32,659 --> 00:32:37,205
Ivy Aguas comes home with us tonight.

481
00:32:37,288 --> 00:32:40,333
[tense music playing]

482
00:32:44,212 --> 00:32:45,129
[sighs]

483
00:32:55,306 --> 00:32:58,101
Grandpa, wait for me.

484
00:33:00,353 --> 00:33:05,358
[tense music playing]

485
00:33:16,661 --> 00:33:18,746
[reporter 1] Congressman, any
statement about what happened?

486
00:33:18,830 --> 00:33:20,289
-What can you say?
-I have nothing to say.

487
00:33:20,373 --> 00:33:22,166
[reporter 1] How's your family doing?

488
00:33:22,500 --> 00:33:24,836
Miss Ivy Aguas, are you
and the mayor on good terms?

489
00:33:24,919 --> 00:33:25,920
I'm sorry, not now.

490
00:33:26,254 --> 00:33:28,881
[reporter 2] Miss Emilia, what
happened to your son, Arnaldo?

491
00:33:29,590 --> 00:33:32,010
Well, yes. It's true
that something happened to him.

492
00:33:32,093 --> 00:33:35,346
The worst thing that can happen
to a mother in distress…

493
00:33:35,638 --> 00:33:38,433
A snake has entered our home.

494
00:33:38,891 --> 00:33:39,892
Emilia.

495
00:33:39,976 --> 00:33:42,603
-[camera shutter clicks]
-I need to ask you something.

496
00:33:44,313 --> 00:33:46,649
[reporter 1] Wait!
When will he leave the hospital?

497
00:33:46,733 --> 00:33:48,693
-[reporter 2] Sir, a statement?
-[reporter 1] Wait!

498
00:33:48,776 --> 00:33:52,113
What was that?!
Was that on purpose, Emilia?!

499
00:33:52,196 --> 00:33:54,115
You're doing this on purpose, Papa!

500
00:33:54,198 --> 00:33:55,241
How can you do this?

501
00:33:55,324 --> 00:33:58,453
How can you let that rat
destroy our family, our home?

502
00:33:58,536 --> 00:33:59,954
Put a lid on it!

503
00:34:01,956 --> 00:34:04,000
Well, it wasn't long ago

504
00:34:04,083 --> 00:34:05,835
that you were so furious with my son!

505
00:34:05,918 --> 00:34:08,004
Even I couldn't believe
the things you said!

506
00:34:08,087 --> 00:34:12,008
That's what you think because
that's what you want to think.

507
00:34:12,633 --> 00:34:14,343
What matters now is Arnaldo.

508
00:34:14,427 --> 00:34:16,387
He's more important than your paranoia.

509
00:34:17,013 --> 00:34:19,849
Or maybe, you want
to follow in his footsteps?

510
00:34:20,183 --> 00:34:22,769
Be careful. You might break.

511
00:34:22,852 --> 00:34:24,228
[scoffs] The nerve!

512
00:34:24,812 --> 00:34:28,316
Papa, how can you protect her like this?

513
00:34:28,399 --> 00:34:29,650
This woman?

514
00:34:30,068 --> 00:34:33,196
She's forcing herself
to be one of us, Papa.

515
00:34:33,279 --> 00:34:35,656
And she's never going
to be one of us, Papa!

516
00:34:35,740 --> 00:34:38,993
Your son needs Ivy.

517
00:34:40,203 --> 00:34:43,498
Without Ivy, Arnaldo will die.

518
00:34:44,082 --> 00:34:46,667
So, if you don't want to lose Arnaldo,

519
00:34:47,293 --> 00:34:52,006
you will kill whatever demons
are whispering in your ears

520
00:34:52,090 --> 00:34:56,385
and you will accept the fact
that Miss Aguas is here to stay.

521
00:35:00,556 --> 00:35:03,476
And you will do that, Emilia…

522
00:35:04,227 --> 00:35:06,938
if you want your son to live.

523
00:35:11,317 --> 00:35:14,987
[tense music playing]

524
00:35:18,616 --> 00:35:19,784
[sighs]

525
00:35:22,328 --> 00:35:24,080
I'm sorry, Congressman.

526
00:35:24,664 --> 00:35:27,083
She never understands anything anyway.

527
00:35:30,461 --> 00:35:31,337
[sighs]

528
00:35:34,507 --> 00:35:37,593
Auntie, does Lily really need
to go back to the Ardientes?

529
00:35:38,344 --> 00:35:41,139
It's dangerous.
She's using herself as bait.

530
00:35:41,389 --> 00:35:44,559
They can't hurt her
or lay a finger on her.

531
00:35:45,309 --> 00:35:46,853
Anna, Lily is smart.

532
00:35:46,936 --> 00:35:48,604
She can manipulate the Ardientes

533
00:35:48,688 --> 00:35:51,065
even if Arnaldo isn't in the mansion.

534
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:52,900
I'm just concerned, Auntie.

535
00:35:52,984 --> 00:35:56,654
Arnaldo's crimes
have already been made public.

536
00:35:57,155 --> 00:35:59,532
But his case was just dismissed
like it was nothing.

537
00:35:59,615 --> 00:36:01,492
Auntie, don't we have
any chances to fight this?

538
00:36:01,576 --> 00:36:03,953
Fighting the Ardientes isn't that easy.

539
00:36:04,829 --> 00:36:05,913
No.

540
00:36:05,997 --> 00:36:08,916
We need that demon, Arnaldo,
to answer for his crimes.

541
00:36:09,834 --> 00:36:13,504
If not through the law,
then maybe there's another way.

542
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:17,884
[tense music playing]

543
00:36:19,886 --> 00:36:20,970
[Emilia] So, Ivy…

544
00:36:21,387 --> 00:36:25,224
Since Arnaldo isn't here at the moment…

545
00:36:26,809 --> 00:36:28,644
Are you willing to mingle with us?

546
00:36:29,061 --> 00:36:30,313
[Julio] Emilia…

547
00:36:31,105 --> 00:36:33,774
Now that Miss Aguas is back with us,

548
00:36:34,734 --> 00:36:37,320
I would advise you to bite your tongue

549
00:36:37,403 --> 00:36:38,863
every time you get the urge

550
00:36:38,946 --> 00:36:41,449
to hurl invectives or insults at her.

551
00:36:41,532 --> 00:36:42,533
[scoffs]

552
00:36:42,617 --> 00:36:46,579
Miss Aguas is here as a favor for Arnaldo.

553
00:36:46,662 --> 00:36:48,748
So, please, respect her.

554
00:36:49,582 --> 00:36:51,292
I respect her, Papa.

555
00:36:51,375 --> 00:36:53,002
I just don't like her.

556
00:36:55,129 --> 00:36:57,548
I really do respect you…

557
00:36:58,466 --> 00:37:03,387
to a point where I won't
drag you out of our home.

558
00:37:03,471 --> 00:37:04,764
So, I'll give way.

559
00:37:04,847 --> 00:37:06,390
I'll leave, instead.

560
00:37:06,474 --> 00:37:07,975
Excuse me.

561
00:37:12,688 --> 00:37:14,482
[shrieks] Oh my…

562
00:37:14,565 --> 00:37:17,026
-[house help] I'm so sorry!
-You idiot! Idiot!

563
00:37:17,902 --> 00:37:19,487
-Emilia!
-[Emilia] You idiot!

564
00:37:19,570 --> 00:37:21,656
-Where's your brain, huh?!
-[house help] I'm sorry!

565
00:37:21,739 --> 00:37:23,991
You want this, right? Here, eat it!

566
00:37:24,075 --> 00:37:25,409
-[Raul] Emilia, that's enough.
-[Claire] Emilia!

567
00:37:25,493 --> 00:37:28,621
And always remember,
you don't belong here!

568
00:37:28,704 --> 00:37:30,414
Do you understand?!

569
00:37:31,040 --> 00:37:32,917
-What an idiot.
-That's enough.

570
00:37:36,712 --> 00:37:38,297
[Emilia] This is expensive!

571
00:37:38,381 --> 00:37:40,675
This is worth more than
what you're paid, you idiot!

572
00:37:41,550 --> 00:37:43,052
<i>Go on, Emilia.</i>

573
00:37:43,135 --> 00:37:46,722
<i>Enjoy yourself while you still can</i>

574
00:37:46,806 --> 00:37:48,474
<i>because the day will come</i>

575
00:37:48,557 --> 00:37:51,185
<i>when what I'm going to do</i>
<i>to you will be worse.</i>

576
00:37:51,269 --> 00:37:54,313
<i>I will make you eat dirt.</i>

577
00:37:54,397 --> 00:37:55,564
<i>Dirt.</i>

578
00:38:03,990 --> 00:38:05,950
Anna, I understand how you feel.

579
00:38:06,909 --> 00:38:10,413
But we need to follow
and trust Lily's plans.

580
00:38:10,997 --> 00:38:13,040
Diego, I have a lot of faith in Lily.

581
00:38:13,124 --> 00:38:14,333
There's no doubt about that.

582
00:38:14,875 --> 00:38:17,712
But that faith is clashing
with the thought

583
00:38:17,795 --> 00:38:20,631
that Arnaldo is still alive and free.

584
00:38:22,174 --> 00:38:23,968
Diego, where's the justice in that?

585
00:38:26,262 --> 00:38:29,140
Who said justice was easy to get?

586
00:38:30,182 --> 00:38:31,767
Let me tell you, Anna,

587
00:38:31,851 --> 00:38:34,979
justice isn't something you buy
at a discount.

588
00:38:36,731 --> 00:38:38,399
I crippled Arnaldo.

589
00:38:38,482 --> 00:38:44,113
He isn't free since
he's imprisoned by his insanity.

590
00:38:45,656 --> 00:38:47,491
Now, what are you doing here?

591
00:38:48,117 --> 00:38:49,368
Didn't we have an agreement?

592
00:38:50,077 --> 00:38:53,205
That on the day of my wedding,
you're going to leave.

593
00:38:53,289 --> 00:38:54,582
But I let it go.

594
00:38:56,459 --> 00:38:58,961
Now, what are you still doing here?

595
00:39:01,464 --> 00:39:04,300
I want to trust in your justice, Lily.

596
00:39:06,927 --> 00:39:08,929
But I'm not leaving.

597
00:39:09,180 --> 00:39:12,224
I want to see that justice delivered.

598
00:39:12,308 --> 00:39:15,019
[tense music playing]

599
00:39:15,269 --> 00:39:19,940
Lily, I held myself back.
I didn't say a word

600
00:39:20,024 --> 00:39:22,943
when you kept your plans
for Arnaldo a secret.

601
00:39:25,821 --> 00:39:27,698
Now that you're going after Emilia,

602
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:31,994
it's my right as your mother
to know about all your plans.

603
00:39:32,787 --> 00:39:34,580
Are you still pursuing them?

604
00:39:35,873 --> 00:39:37,708
Mom, nothing has changed.

605
00:39:37,792 --> 00:39:39,919
I'll pursue my plans for Emilia.

606
00:39:40,878 --> 00:39:44,507
I'll strip her of her wealth
and family name.

607
00:39:45,466 --> 00:39:47,009
Then I'll help you, Lily.

608
00:39:47,968 --> 00:39:50,429
We'll take down Emilia.

609
00:39:50,971 --> 00:39:52,431
I'll help too, Lily.

610
00:39:55,309 --> 00:39:56,477
No, you won't.

611
00:39:57,395 --> 00:40:00,856
Anna, you knew from the start
I was against you being here

612
00:40:00,940 --> 00:40:02,983
because I don't want to put you in danger.

613
00:40:03,067 --> 00:40:04,777
So, I hope you understand.

614
00:40:08,114 --> 00:40:12,243
[tense music playing]

615
00:40:14,203 --> 00:40:15,996
Arnaldo is still alive…

616
00:40:17,331 --> 00:40:20,292
but he's mentally
and emotionally unstable.

617
00:40:21,710 --> 00:40:24,296
I'm sure that the Ardientes
will do everything

618
00:40:24,713 --> 00:40:29,093
for Arnaldo to get well but
I won't make it easy for them.

619
00:40:29,176 --> 00:40:33,055
I won't let Arnaldo
get back on his feet again.

620
00:40:33,431 --> 00:40:37,435
[tense music playing]

621
00:40:47,194 --> 00:40:49,113
[humming]

622
00:40:54,410 --> 00:40:57,413
[foreboding music playing]

623
00:41:08,132 --> 00:41:09,133
Hmm.

624
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:12,428
Oh, Jaguar…

625
00:41:14,096 --> 00:41:15,139
[exhales]

626
00:41:16,891 --> 00:41:18,058
[line ringing]

627
00:41:28,861 --> 00:41:29,862
[line ringing]

628
00:41:30,779 --> 00:41:32,239
Hello, Jaguar?

629
00:41:33,574 --> 00:41:35,326
Hello, Emilia.

630
00:41:35,868 --> 00:41:38,245
You know, you're really full of surprises.

631
00:41:38,662 --> 00:41:40,539
You actually made my day today.

632
00:41:40,623 --> 00:41:42,249
[scoffs] Surprises?

633
00:41:42,333 --> 00:41:43,083
<i>Yeah.</i>

634
00:41:43,167 --> 00:41:45,836
You sent me flowers and I love it.

635
00:41:46,545 --> 00:41:50,674
I'm just wondering how you knew
that roses are my favorite.

636
00:41:50,758 --> 00:41:52,551
I didn't send you flowers.

637
00:41:52,635 --> 00:41:53,969
<i>They're not from me.</i>

638
00:41:54,053 --> 00:41:55,054
What?

639
00:42:01,268 --> 00:42:02,686
They're from Raul?

640
00:42:03,062 --> 00:42:06,357
Hold on. Why do you seem surprised?

641
00:42:06,440 --> 00:42:08,275
<i>Aren't you supposed to be glad?</i>

642
00:42:08,359 --> 00:42:10,945
You told me that you
still love your husband.

643
00:42:13,697 --> 00:42:16,992
Because Raul can't please me with flowers.

644
00:42:17,076 --> 00:42:20,996
Anything that comes from him
is trash, cheap, and ugly!

645
00:42:21,080 --> 00:42:24,375
In fact, I'll throw these
disgusting flowers away.

646
00:42:25,042 --> 00:42:28,045
[tense music playing]

647
00:42:34,468 --> 00:42:35,469
[slams]

648
00:42:41,100 --> 00:42:44,103
[phone vibrating]

649
00:42:50,067 --> 00:42:53,070
Ivy, every second that you're with Arnaldo

650
00:42:53,153 --> 00:42:55,864
is a second less spent with your mother.

651
00:42:57,700 --> 00:43:01,537
Ivy, please stop this.
You're in too deep now.

652
00:43:02,413 --> 00:43:05,874
Diego, taking care of Arnaldo is my key

653
00:43:05,958 --> 00:43:08,752
to gaining access
to the Ardientes' mansion

654
00:43:08,836 --> 00:43:11,589
and pursuing my plans to take down Emilia.

655
00:43:11,672 --> 00:43:15,050
What if he actually gets better
under your care?

656
00:43:15,426 --> 00:43:18,053
I won't let that happen. Never.

657
00:43:19,054 --> 00:43:20,931
I know it's not easy…

658
00:43:21,348 --> 00:43:23,642
and my plans aren't
that clear and perfect,

659
00:43:23,726 --> 00:43:25,269
but I've taken Arnaldo out.

660
00:43:25,728 --> 00:43:27,855
And now, Emilia has to go next.

661
00:43:28,355 --> 00:43:33,986
I won't waste any time
in bringing that woman down.

662
00:43:34,820 --> 00:43:35,821
[sighs]

663
00:43:38,032 --> 00:43:39,908
Just be careful, okay?

664
00:43:40,618 --> 00:43:42,578
Ivy, please take care of yourself.

665
00:43:43,954 --> 00:43:47,458
[unsettling music playing]

666
00:43:49,126 --> 00:43:53,255
[monitor beeping rhythmically]

667
00:43:53,672 --> 00:43:56,550
I have issued a press release

668
00:43:56,884 --> 00:43:59,011
and I'm doing
the necessary damage control.

669
00:43:59,553 --> 00:44:03,474
Thank you for your initiative
and foresight, Miss Aguas.

670
00:44:05,726 --> 00:44:06,685
Emilia…

671
00:44:07,645 --> 00:44:12,107
Why don't you help Miss Aguas
with the damage control

672
00:44:12,191 --> 00:44:14,151
and make yourself useful?

673
00:44:14,526 --> 00:44:16,487
Papa, I'd rather not say anything.

674
00:44:16,737 --> 00:44:22,326
I can't work very well with
people who get on my nerves.

675
00:44:25,162 --> 00:44:27,831
We're on the same side, Emilia.

676
00:44:29,166 --> 00:44:30,626
We both want Arnaldo to recover.

677
00:44:31,669 --> 00:44:33,337
I hope we're on the same page.

678
00:44:34,838 --> 00:44:37,966
[tense music playing]

679
00:44:38,509 --> 00:44:41,053
[reporter] What can you say
about the recent hospitalization

680
00:44:41,136 --> 00:44:42,805
-of Mayor Ardiente?
-[camera shutters click]

681
00:44:43,222 --> 00:44:45,849
I'm saddened by the news about the mayor.

682
00:44:46,433 --> 00:44:47,685
After all, he's my brother.

683
00:44:48,143 --> 00:44:53,023
But that doesn't mean we won't
reopen the lawsuits against him.

684
00:44:53,107 --> 00:44:57,027
Homicide for the murders
of Nimfa, Carlotta,

685
00:44:57,111 --> 00:44:58,737
and Camia Cruz's witnesses.

686
00:44:58,821 --> 00:45:01,115
This is something
we can't take just sitting down.

687
00:45:01,198 --> 00:45:02,491
We'll rise back up

688
00:45:02,991 --> 00:45:07,830
and file the case at a different
court with a different judge.

689
00:45:07,913 --> 00:45:10,457
We won't stop until
Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo

690
00:45:10,541 --> 00:45:12,584
pays for what he did.

691
00:45:12,918 --> 00:45:16,171
So, to Mayor Arnaldo and his allies,

692
00:45:16,880 --> 00:45:19,258
you may have succeeded
in having the case dismissed,

693
00:45:19,341 --> 00:45:22,970
but that doesn't change the fact
that you're still guilty.

694
00:45:25,013 --> 00:45:26,974
Karma is on our side…

695
00:45:27,307 --> 00:45:29,017
and you'll pay a very high price.

696
00:45:32,980 --> 00:45:34,189
We have some good news.

697
00:45:34,648 --> 00:45:37,276
The results of his tests
and x-ray are normal.

698
00:45:37,693 --> 00:45:40,529
And we'll observe him
for the next 24 hours.

699
00:45:40,612 --> 00:45:44,908
After that, we expect him
to regain full consciousness.

700
00:45:44,992 --> 00:45:46,952
Attaboy, Arnaldo.

701
00:45:47,035 --> 00:45:48,579
You go and fight.

702
00:45:49,079 --> 00:45:50,330
[doctor] And when he wakes up,

703
00:45:50,414 --> 00:45:54,168
we can start his psychiatric
counseling and therapy.

704
00:45:54,668 --> 00:45:56,462
So, in short, doc…

705
00:45:57,379 --> 00:45:59,756
he'll recover easily? I mean…

706
00:46:00,215 --> 00:46:03,051
Is one week good enough
for him to recover?

707
00:46:03,969 --> 00:46:08,724
Papa, Arnaldo needs to pass all his tests…

708
00:46:08,807 --> 00:46:11,310
and get clearance from the doctor.

709
00:46:12,936 --> 00:46:16,064
We do not have the time, Emilia.

710
00:46:16,690 --> 00:46:18,192
He has an election to win.

711
00:46:20,027 --> 00:46:22,404
Doc, maybe it's best…

712
00:46:22,654 --> 00:46:25,782
if you prescribe all the
medicine Arnaldo needs to take.

713
00:46:25,866 --> 00:46:28,494
We are going to make sure
he takes all of it.

714
00:46:29,953 --> 00:46:33,248
Grandpa… I get where you're coming from.

715
00:46:33,707 --> 00:46:35,834
You want Arnaldo
to have a speedy recovery.

716
00:46:35,918 --> 00:46:39,171
But, we need to give him time
to recuperate,

717
00:46:39,254 --> 00:46:42,799
so we can make sure
he'll really win the election.

718
00:46:43,050 --> 00:46:47,054
[tense music playing]

719
00:47:04,363 --> 00:47:05,572
Wait a minute, Emilia.

720
00:47:06,031 --> 00:47:07,449
What's going on?

721
00:47:07,866 --> 00:47:09,284
Do you really want an annulment

722
00:47:09,368 --> 00:47:11,453
while our son's fighting for his life?

723
00:47:11,537 --> 00:47:14,206
Please Raul, can you not use
our son's condition

724
00:47:14,289 --> 00:47:15,582
to settle our problems?

725
00:47:15,666 --> 00:47:16,959
I want an annulment.

726
00:47:17,042 --> 00:47:19,002
To begin with, our marriage is fake.

727
00:47:19,086 --> 00:47:21,463
[scoffs] Why? Who's real to you?

728
00:47:21,964 --> 00:47:24,091
Tell me… Is it Jaguar?

729
00:47:25,092 --> 00:47:26,093
He's just fooling you.

730
00:47:26,176 --> 00:47:29,596
If he really loved you…
he would've fought for you.

731
00:47:29,680 --> 00:47:32,599
You know, Raul, the reason
why you're chasing me

732
00:47:32,683 --> 00:47:34,268
is because somebody else wants me.

733
00:47:34,810 --> 00:47:35,811
After 30 years,

734
00:47:35,894 --> 00:47:38,814
not even once did I feel
you truly loved me, Raul.

735
00:47:38,897 --> 00:47:39,982
Not even once.

736
00:47:40,065 --> 00:47:42,526
So, please, can you not be selfish?

737
00:47:42,609 --> 00:47:45,320
I'm not selfish. That's why I'm trying.

738
00:47:45,404 --> 00:47:46,989
Give me a chance.

739
00:47:47,072 --> 00:47:48,323
Just sign the document.

740
00:47:48,407 --> 00:47:51,702
I want the annulment,
and we're done. It's over.

741
00:47:56,623 --> 00:47:57,916
Damn it.

742
00:48:03,046 --> 00:48:04,423
Hello, Natalie?

743
00:48:04,506 --> 00:48:07,050
[Natalie] <i>Thank goodness.</i>
<i>Finally, you answered my call.</i>

744
00:48:07,134 --> 00:48:09,386
I've been trying to call you
and you don't answer.

745
00:48:09,928 --> 00:48:13,932
-What do you need from me?
-<i>Me? Need something from you?</i>

746
00:48:14,433 --> 00:48:17,644
[sighs] Raul, that's not
the story of our relationship.

747
00:48:17,728 --> 00:48:21,189
It's more of you
needing something from me.

748
00:48:21,273 --> 00:48:24,860
And in this case, I know
you want something from me.

749
00:48:25,402 --> 00:48:28,238
I don't understand.
What are you talking about?

750
00:48:28,322 --> 00:48:31,450
[Natalie] <i>I saw that Arnaldo</i>
<i>is getting sick.</i>

751
00:48:31,533 --> 00:48:34,786
And I'm sure that stresses
you out so much.

752
00:48:34,870 --> 00:48:38,790
So, I'm offering you
a de-stressing kind of session.

753
00:48:39,916 --> 00:48:43,378
Let's not kid ourselves.
This is going once…

754
00:48:43,462 --> 00:48:44,671
twice…

755
00:48:45,172 --> 00:48:47,299
Fine, eight o'clock. The usual place.

756
00:48:47,382 --> 00:48:49,968
I can't wait to see you. Bye!

757
00:48:57,934 --> 00:49:01,396
[tense music playing]

758
00:49:18,747 --> 00:49:20,540
[Ivy] <i>I have information.</i>

759
00:49:20,624 --> 00:49:23,293
<i>And I know you'll be interested.</i>

760
00:49:23,377 --> 00:49:27,214
<i>I will crush that woman into pieces.</i>

761
00:49:27,297 --> 00:49:28,465
-<i>Surprise.</i>
-[chuckles]

762
00:49:28,548 --> 00:49:29,800
-[thwacks]
-[grunts]

763
00:49:29,883 --> 00:49:33,595
[Anna] <i>Do you know how long</i>
<i>I've waited for this opportunity?</i>

764
00:49:33,679 --> 00:49:38,600
<i>Hatred and the need for revenge</i>
<i>can change a person a lot.</i>

765
00:49:39,726 --> 00:49:42,229
